  "details": "I'm currently dealing with a problem where I have to detect if you're in the scaling menu, The problem is, is that there's no real good way to do that. It would be great to have an \"Is Scaling\" parameter, because I can detect stuff like \"ScaleModified\", but not if the avatar is actively being scaled. Like, an example. You know the normal radial puppets? They have a place where you can put a parameter like a bool as an example, and it effectively tells you if the radial puppet menu is open. I want something like that for scaling, so when you're in that menu, it turns a bool to true.",
